WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.449
Welcome to Starling.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.192
We begin with an empty desktop. Open the control panel, and choose Three D Desktop.

3
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.648
The city is now your workspace.

4
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:33.412
Before opening any apps, let's explore. Walk down the hill, past the houses, toward the waterfront.

5
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.263
At the seaside, take a moment to watch the ferry move across the bay.

6
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.456
Now, back to the overlook.

7
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.133
Let's build a workspace with just four apps. Start with Chrome, and browse the web.

8
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.346
Switch to full screen for a closer look, then return to the city.

9
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.141
Next, open Video Player, and choose a film.

10
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.242
Big Buck Bunny plays in its own window, with a live preview on the rail.

11
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.012
Open Files to browse your folders.

12
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.279
Then launch Terminal, and run a command. All four apps share the same workspace.

13
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:30.907
Hold Alt and press Tab to bring up the window switcher. Move between Chrome, Video Player, Files, and Terminal.

14
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.708
One city. Four apps. Your workspace.
